 <link>https://telegram.org/dl/osx</link>
 <item>
 <title>Telegram macOS</title>
+<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• Widgets now run on Nova, a JavaScript engine in Rust with every unsafe operation removed for protection, so a widget's script can't corrupt memory; it runs inside the sandboxed widget process, and QuickJS no longer runs widget code&lt;br&gt;• The widget checker runs on Nova too, and the widget process refuses any other engine&lt;br&gt;• Beta updates now list what changed, taken from the pushed changes&lt;br&gt;• Widgets can be drawn in a separate sandboxed process as well (debug switch, off by default)&lt;br&gt;• The brain in an AI task bubble can be grabbed and pulled until it tears&lt;br&gt;• Letters flying into the black hole while a conversation is compacted bend toward the pointer&lt;br&gt;• Photos, videos, files and other media are stored encrypted on this Mac&lt;br&gt;• Encrypted exports open in a browser with a password Telegram shows once&lt;br&gt;• A strength meter under a new passcode while you type it&lt;br&gt;• The emoji panel is built from your Mac's emoji font, so new emoji appear after a macOS update without updating Telegram&lt;br&gt;• Some rarely used animations and 3D scenes download after you log in instead of shipping with the app&lt;br&gt;• Redesigned profiles with a new photo layout, interactive gifts, and an updated music player&lt;br&gt;• Lockdown Mode settings: choose Allow, Ask or Never for chats with non-contacts, bots, media, files, links, mini apps, web content, payments, destructive actions and the assistant&lt;br&gt;• The assistant connect screen shows the Dictator logo and name&lt;br&gt;• Mention your Dictator bot in any chat to ask the agent there, once Guest Mode is on in @BotFather (Open → your bot → Settings → Guest Mode)&lt;br&gt;• Ask the agent for the Stars history of your bots and channels, or export it to a spreadsheet&lt;br&gt;• On-device speech: dictation, voice message transcription and live call captions can run on your Mac with downloadable speech models.&lt;br&gt;• Settings &gt; Data and Storage &gt; On-Device Speech manages speech languages, local voice transcription and the downloaded models.&lt;br&gt;• The gift marketplace shows your balance in a glass pill, as on iOS; with Grams it opens a My Stars / My Grams menu.&lt;br&gt;• Opening a profile from the chat header flies the avatar into the profile and back.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• Stronger protection of local data: passcode-protected database key, encrypted AI assistant storage, Mini App secrets kept per account&lt;br&gt;• Telegram's local data is now always encrypted with a key kept in this Mac's Keychain, even without a passcode, so a copy of its files can't be read elsewhere&lt;br&gt;• Log Out on the passcode screen now erases the data stored on this Mac right away&lt;br&gt;• The passcode screen shows progress while it checks your passcode and pauses briefly after a wrong one&lt;br&gt;• Hovering a widget no longer makes Telegram parse the widget's HTML itself&lt;br&gt;• Widgets drawn in the separate process: smooth frames at the display's rate, steady while a message changes height, ready before they scroll into view, much less memory, animations at 60 frames a second, and a restart if that process ends&lt;br&gt;• Bot HTML documents, including tall ones and 3D, can be drawn in the separate process too (same debug switch)&lt;br&gt;• Widgets start as fast as before the new engine: its startup code is compiled once and shared&lt;br&gt;• A redesigned Optimizing Database screen that fades into your chats&lt;br&gt;• Widgets run about 30% faster on the new engine; heavy widgets are no longer stopped by the time limit&lt;br&gt;• A widget can no longer stall the widget process while its script is being read&lt;br&gt;• Photos, avatars, stickers, GIFs and other images are decoded in a separate sandboxed process, so a malicious image can't reach Telegram's memory, and a screen of photos appears about 20% faster&lt;br&gt;• Animated stickers and emoji are drawn in a separate sandboxed process, so a malicious animation can't reach Telegram's memory&lt;br&gt;• Code blocks are highlighted in a separate sandboxed process: a malicious or huge code block can't crash or freeze Telegram&lt;br&gt;</description>
+<pubDate>2026-20-11 18:37:32</pubDate>
